# Sources used:
# - Wikipedia, Windward Caribbean Kulture page (opened 2026-10-20): WCK formed in 1988 in Dominica, bouyon blend of cadence-lypso and jing ping, strong emphasis on keyboard rhythmic patterns; former band members list includes "Earlson Matthew a.k.a Likkle Man....lead Keyboardist" and Delton Alfred a.k.a "Delly" (Lead Vocals) and Keith Goddard on bass guitar.
# - A Virtual Dominica, Bouyon in Dominica page (opened 2026-10-20): WCK created bouyon as a fusion of cadence-lypso and traditional jing ping, the sequencing of the prominent keyboards is an integral part of the bouyon sound; current band members list includes Keith Goddard, Earlson Matthew, Albert Lockhart, Delton Alfred, Marsha Augustine, Shannon Liverpool and Nehimiah Darroux. Older community site, reported as a roster listing.
# - Wikipedia, Caribbean Community page, Song section (opened 2026-10-20, Earlson found at line 697): for CARICOM 40th anniversary a competition launched in April 2013 condensed 63 entries to a final three; judges chose "Celebrating CARICOM" by Michele Henderson of Dominica in March 2014; Henderson won US$10,000; the song was produced by her husband Roland Delsol Jr. and arranged by Earlson Matthew, featured Michael Ferrol on drums and choral input from the St. Alphonsus Choir, and was re-produced for CARICOM by Carl Beaver Henderson of Trinidad and Tobago; first official performance on Tuesday 1 July 2014 at the opening ceremony of the Thirty-Fifth Meeting of the Conference of Heads of Government in Antigua and Barbuda.
# - YouTube, How De Band Playing - Mr Delly x Likkle Man - Bouyon 2023 (opened 2026-10-20): description explains the old saying "How the band, is so you have to dance" and its application to life situations beyond our control; credits: written and composed by Earlson "Likkle Man" Matthew, performed by Delton "Mr. Delly" Alfred, bass Elijah JeanJacques, guitar Joel Francis, drums Nikita "Fridge" Christmas, additional vocals Erneil "Shabba" Paul, Dorelle Diolen, Serena Alexander, Syan Davis, Deanna Emmanuel and Michael "Bully/ Ti Mal" John, recorded and mixed at Sonic Art Studios; keywords tie the record to bouyon, bouyon soca, Dominica and Dominica Carnival 2023.
# - YouTube, To The City - Likkle Man X Peter Pros (opened 2026-10-20): composed by Earlson "Likkle Man" Matthew, performed by Peter Prospere, guitar Monelle "High Speed" Mondesire, bass Keith Goddard, recorded, mixed and mastered at Sonic Art Studios by Earlson "Likkle Man" Matthew, graphic design Kester Labad; keywords tie the record to bouyon, WCK, Dominica, WCMF and Triple Kay circles.
# - Discover Dominica Authority press release, Bouyon Day 2025 (PDF, opened 2026-10-20): Bouyon in de Streets, free event on Tuesday 25 February 2025, 6 PM to midnight, Hanover Street, Roseau; lineup billed as bouyon icons includes Likkle Man alongside Asa Bantan, Litle Boy, Quan, Reo, Freddy, Clint H, Najee, Skinny Bantan, Rah, Delly, Kenny G and TK International, with Unstoppable Shax and DJ Snow.
