    "The keywords published with the record place “To The City” at the centre of the current bouyon map: bouyon, bouyon music, WCK, Dominica, Likkle Man, Triple Kay, Ridge, Mr Benji, Delly, WCMF and World Creole Music Festival. Those keywords are publishing tags, not credits, and this profile treats them as such: they show in which neighbourhood the record wants to be found, that of the bands and singers of Dominican bouyon today, without proving a collaboration with each name cited.",
    "Taken together, “How De Band Playing” and “To The City” draw the working method of the musician in the 2020s: write for the voices of others, gather a small band of regulars, record at Sonic Art Studios, and, when the record requires it, handle the mixing and mastering himself. It is workshop work, far from the posters, but it is what turns a street proverb and a keyboard composition into released carnival records. The context of the festival where this bouyon is played each October is read on our <a href=\"/en/world-creole-music-festival.html\">World Creole Music Festival</a> page."
